  "source": "The Public Health Agency of Sweden",
  "note": [
    "Indicator definition: Percentage (%) of the population (16–84 years or 16 years and older) that has used e-cigarettes or e-cigarettes containing nicotine. Percentage reported by region, gender and years (4 year mean values). Response rate for the Swedish National Public Health Survey: 2018 (42,1 %), 2020 (42,3 %), 2021 (44,1 %), 2022 (37,9 %), 2024 (39,4 %). The survey is conducted every two years. In 2021, an extra round of the survey was conducted due to the ongoing corona pandemic."
